Microplastic particles have also been classified according to their type, which included beads, foams, pellets, fibers and fragments (Dodson et al., 2020; Qi et al., 2020; Saborowski et al., 2019). Polymers used to manufacture microplastics include polystyrene, polyvinyl chloride, polyethylene, polyether sulfone, low-density polyethylene, high-density polyethylene, polyethylene terephthalate, polypropylene, cellulose acetate, polyamide, polyacrylates, and polyester (Welden, 2019; Welden and Lusher, 2020; Wong et al., 2020). Higher concentrations of microplastics were commonly discharged from WWTPs due to fishing related operations and laundries.

